'''''Anthony Bourdain: Parts Unknown''''' is an American travel and food show on [[CNN]] that premiered on April 14, 2013. In the show, [[Anthony Bourdain]] travels the world uncovering lesser-known places and exploring their cultures and cuisine.<ref>{{cite web |title=Anthony Bourdain: Parts Unknown - CNN |url=http://zeropointzero.com/tv/ |website=Zero Point Zero Productions |access-date=February 18, 2015 |url-status=dead |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20150217063154/http://zeropointzero.com/tv/ |archive-date=February 17, 2015}}</ref> The show won twelve [[Primetime Emmy Awards]] out of 31 nominations, as well as a 2013 [[Peabody Award]].<ref>{{cite web |title=Anthony Bourdain: Parts Unknown |url=http://www.emmys.com/shows/anthony-bourdain-parts-unknown |website=Television Academy |access-date=January 28, 2016}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |last1=Shah |first1=Khushbu |title=Anthony Bourdain's Parts Unknown Wins Another Emmy |url=http://www.eater.com/2014/8/18/6169541/anthony-bourdains-parts-unknown-wins-another-emmy |website=Eater  |date=August 18, 2014 |access-date=February 18, 2015}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |title=Anthony Bourdain: Parts Unknown (CNN) |url=http://www.peabodyawards.com/award-profile/anthony-bourdain-parts-unknown-cnn |access-date=October 28, 2015}}</ref> 

The digital series Explore Parts Unknown, an editorial partnership with [[Roads & Kingdoms]], won a [[Primetime Emmy Award for Outstanding Short Form Nonfiction or Reality Series]].<ref>{{cite web |title=Anthony Bourdain: Explore Parts Unknown |url=https://www.emmys.com/shows/anthony-bourdain-explore-parts-unknown |website=Television Academy}}</ref> ''Parts Unknown'' aired the last collection of episodes on CNN in the autumn of 2018. The series finale, titled "Lower East Side"—bringing Bourdain's culinary travelogue full circle back to Bourdain's hometown of [[New York City|New York]]—aired November 11, 2018.<ref>{{cite web |url=http://www.latimes.com/business/hollywood/la-fi-ct-cnn-bourdain-20180801-story.html |title=CNN will say goodbye to Anthony Bourdain with a final season this fall |date=August 1, 2018 |first=Stephen |last=Battaglio |website=Los Angeles Times}}</ref>

Bourdain was working on an episode of the show centered in [[Strasbourg]], [[France]], at the time of his death on June 8, 2018.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.cnn.com/2018/06/08/us/anthony-bourdain-obit/index.html |title=CNN's Anthony Bourdain dead at 61 |first=Brian |last=Stelter |publisher=CNN |date=June 8, 2018}}</ref>

