 |Title = Myanmar
 |OriginalAirDate={{Start date|2013|04|14}}
 |ShortSummary=With the [[2011–12 Burmese political reforms|slight relaxation of control]] by the government of Myanmar (Burma), Tony is finally able to explore one of the most fabled and beautiful areas of [[Asia]].
 |LineColor=FFA6B9
}}
{{Episode list
 |EpisodeNumber2=2
 |EpisodeNumber=2
 |Title = Koreatown, Los Angeles
 |OriginalAirDate={{Start date|2013|04|21}}
 |ShortSummary=Tony visits the three square-mile area of [[Los Angeles]] known as [[Koreatown, Los Angeles|Koreatown]], where he finds a tight-knit community still marked by the [[1992 Los Angeles riots|1992 Rodney King riots]]. Tony travels throughout the community with chef [[Roy Choi]] and artist [[David Choe]] to see how much the town has evolved and how other cultures have integrated into Koreatown, and to see what it was like to grow up Korean American.
 |LineColor=FFA6B9
}}
{{Episode list
 |EpisodeNumber2=3
 |EpisodeNumber=3
 |Title = Colombia
 |OriginalAirDate={{Start date|2013|04|28}}
 |ShortSummary=The public face of Colombia has changed immensely over the past ten years and is still changing for the better. Tony will explore several regions of the country from the [[Andean Natural Region, Colombia|mountains]] down to the [[Caribbean Natural Region, Colombia|Caribbean coast]] to the [[Coca|coca leaf]] growing [[Amazon Natural Region, Colombia|inland]] formerly controlled by [[Illegal drug trade in Colombia|drug cartels]].
 |LineColor=FFA6B9
}}
{{Episode list
 |EpisodeNumber2=4
 |EpisodeNumber=4
 |Title = Quebec
 |OriginalAirDate={{Start date|2013|05|05}}
 |ShortSummary=Bourdain travels to the province of [[Quebec]] where he samples local delicacies in [[Montreal]] and [[Quebec City]] and explores ice fishing and beaver hunting and spends time with two of the funniest and most brilliant chefs/restaurateurs in [[Canada]], [[Joe Beef (restaurant)|Joe Beef]]'s Dave McMillan and Fred Morin.
 |LineColor=FFA6B9
}}
{{Episode list
 |EpisodeNumber2=5
 |EpisodeNumber=5
 |Title = Morocco (Tangier)
 |OriginalAirDate={{Start date|2013|05|12}}
 |ShortSummary=Tony explores the "[[Tangier International Zone|Interzone]]", where artists like [[William S. Burroughs|Burroughs]], [[Paul Bowles|Bowles]] and [[the Rolling Stones]] sought escape from western moral prohibitions and the possibilities of great empty spaces.
 |LineColor=FFA6B9
}}
{{Episode list
 |EpisodeNumber2=6
 |EpisodeNumber=6
 |Title = Libya
 |OriginalAirDate={{Start date|2013|05|19}}
 |ShortSummary=Libyan hip-hop, Italian restaurants, tribal allegiances and post-[[2011 Libyan Civil War|war]] uncertainty in Libya. Bourdain looks at the country through personal stories, food—and the music of anti-[[Muammar Gaddafi|Gaddafi]] rapper expats who returned to fight.
 |LineColor=FFA6B9
}}
{{Episode list
 |EpisodeNumber2=7
 |EpisodeNumber=7
 |Title = Peru
 |OriginalAirDate={{Start date|2013|06|02}}
 |ShortSummary=Tony and his friend, world-renowned chef [[Eric Ripert]], explore the far reaches of indigenous [[Andes]] in search of a rare variety of [[Theobroma cacao|wild cocoa]] that is said to be the best in the world. They move from hip, modern [[Lima]] back in time into [[Pre-Columbian era|pre-Columbian]] Peru.
 |LineColor=FFA6B9
}}
{{Episode list
 |EpisodeNumber2=8
 |EpisodeNumber=8
 |Title = Congo
 |OriginalAirDate={{Start date|2013|06|09}}
 |ShortSummary=Tony visits the Democratic Republic of the Congo, the setting of one of his favorite books, [[Joseph Conrad]]'s ''[[Heart of Darkness]]'', and the basis for one of his favorite movies, ''[[Apocalypse Now]]''. He travels up the [[Congo River]] on a boat.
 |LineColor=FFA6B9
}}
}}

===Season 2 (2013)===
{{Episode table |background=#B60000 |overall= |season= |title= |airdate= |country=U.S. |episodes=
