{{Episode list
 |EpisodeNumber2=2
 |EpisodeNumber=10
 |Title = Jerusalem
 |OriginalAirDate={{Start date|2013|09|15}}
 |ShortSummary=The host and crew make their first trip to [[Israel]], the [[West Bank]] and [[Gaza Strip|Gaza]]. While the political situation is often tense between the people living in these areas, Bourdain concentrates on their rich history; food and culture; and spends time with local chefs, home cooks, writers and amateur foodies.
 |LineColor=B60000
}}
{{Episode list
 |EpisodeNumber2=3
 |EpisodeNumber=11
 |Title = Spain
 |OriginalAirDate={{Start date|2013|09|22}}
 |ShortSummary=Anthony explores [[Andalusia|Andalucía]] during [[Holy Week|Semana Santa]] (Holy Week, leading up to [[Easter]]), a time filled with great pageantry and excitement. Featured in this episode is Bourdain's longtime Director of Photography Zach Zamboni, who lives part-time in [[Granada]] and shows the host sights off the beaten path and immerses them in tapas culture.
 |LineColor=B60000
}}
{{Episode list
 |EpisodeNumber2=4
 |EpisodeNumber=12
 |Title = New Mexico
 |OriginalAirDate={{Start date|2013|09|29}}
 |ShortSummary=The show takes a close look at the mash-up of cultures that comprise this uniquely American state. Tony and crew sample [[New Mexican cuisine|New Mexico's food]] — a combination of [[Spanish cuisine|Spanish]], [[Mediterranean cuisine|Mediterranean]], [[Mexican cuisine|Mexican]], [[Pueblo]], and even [[Chuckwagon|chuck-wagon]] influences. New Mexico is also a land of drugs, guns, monster vehicles, and possibly extraterrestrials. It may also be the perfect place to investigate the underside of the Western cowboy ideal.
 |LineColor=B60000
}}
{{Episode list
 |EpisodeNumber2=5
 |EpisodeNumber=13
 |Title = Copenhagen
 |OriginalAirDate={{Start date|2013|10|06}}
 |ShortSummary=This episode explores the food and natural beauty of Copenhagen, the economic and cultural center of [[Denmark]]. The episode focuses on chef [[René Redzepi]] and his Michelin two star restaurant, [[Noma (restaurant)|Noma]]. Noma was ranked as "[[The World's 50 Best Restaurants|The Best Restaurant in the World]]" in 2010, 2011, and 2012 by [[Restaurant (magazine)|''Restaurant'' magazine]].
 |LineColor=B60000
}}
{{Episode list
 |EpisodeNumber2=6
 |EpisodeNumber=14
 |Title = Sicily
 |OriginalAirDate={{Start date|2013|10|13}}
 |ShortSummary=''Parts Unknown'' explores the Sicilian way of life, which puts a premium on savoring family, life, and [[Sicilian cuisine|food]]. Bourdain travels in search of those foods as he eats his way around the island. He makes his home base at the Villa Monaci, on the outskirts of [[Catania]] with his enthusiastic, fast-talking sidekicks who counter the otherwise relaxed tempo and epic "food porn" of this episode.
 |LineColor=B60000
}}
{{Episode list
 |EpisodeNumber2=7
 |EpisodeNumber=15
 |Title = South Africa
 |OriginalAirDate={{Start date|2013|10|20}}
 |ShortSummary=Once considered the most dangerous city in the world, [[Johannesburg]] now barely makes the top 50. But the end of the [[apartheid]] has led to vast changes in the city.
 |LineColor=B60000
}}
{{Episode list
 |EpisodeNumber2=8
 |EpisodeNumber=16
 |Title = Tokyo
 |OriginalAirDate={{Start date|2013|11|03}}
 |ShortSummary=Bourdain has traveled to Tokyo countless times, but on this trip he is in search of the city's dark, extreme, and bizarrely fetishistic underside. Japan is a paradox. The low birthrate, the dedication, the conformity, and the life of a salary man are well known. There is also a competitive and rigid culture that gives way to some unique subcultures. A significant portion of the episode is spent with sushi chef Yasuda.
 |LineColor=B60000
}}
{{Episode list
 |EpisodeNumber2=9
 |EpisodeNumber=17
 |Title = Detroit
 |OriginalAirDate={{Start date|2013|11|10}}
 |ShortSummary=Bourdain steps into the lives of Detroit natives and sees the glory days of the past at the famed [[Packard Automotive Plant|Packard Plant]], the current state of [[Decline of Detroit|the city's urban decay]], and the promise of the future in the citizens who are rebuilding their communities.
 |LineColor=B60000
}}
}}

===Season 3 (2014)===
