===Season 8 (2016)===
Season 8 aired from September to December 2016, and notably features an interview with U.S. president [[Barack Obama]].<ref>{{cite web |url=http://cnnpressroom.blogs.cnn.com/2016/09/06/a-trip-to-hanoi-featuring-dinner-with-president-obama-kicks-off-season-eight-of-cnn-original-series-anthony-bourdain-parts-unknown-sunday-sept-25-at-9pm/ |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160907140304/http://cnnpressroom.blogs.cnn.com/2016/09/06/a-trip-to-hanoi-featuring-dinner-with-president-obama-kicks-off-season-eight-of-cnn-original-series-anthony-bourdain-parts-unknown-sunday-sept-25-at-9pm/ |url-status=dead |archive-date=September 7, 2016 |title=A Trip to Hanoi, Featuring Dinner with President Obama, Kicks off Season Eight of CNN Original Series Anthony Bourdain Parts Unknown, Sunday Sept. 25 at 9pm |access-date=September 7, 2016 |date=September 7, 2016 |publisher=[[CNN]]}}</ref> Episode 8 (Buenos Aires) was originally scheduled as the Season 7 finale, but was pre-empted by coverage of the [[Orlando nightclub shooting]].

