===Season 10 (2017)===
Season 10 premiered on October 1, 2017.<ref>{{cite web |url=http://www.cnncreativemarketing.com/project/anthony-bourdain-parts-unknown-season-10/ |title=Anthony Bourdain Parts Unknown Season 10 |website=CNNCreativeMarketing.com |access-date=October 28, 2017}}</ref> In the premiere, Bourdain traveled to [[Singapore]]. Other locations include the [[French Alps]], [[Lagos]], [[Pittsburgh]], [[Sri Lanka]], [[Puerto Rico]], [[Seattle]], and [[Southern Italy]].<ref>{{cite web |url=http://www.foodandwine.com/chefs/anthony-bourdain-parts-unknown-season-10-behind-scenes |title=Anthony Bourdain Parts Unknown Season 10: 'It's the Funniest, Filthiest, Most Off-Brand Thing We've Done to Date' |website=FoodAndWine.com |access-date=October 28, 2017}}</ref> On November 12, 2017, the show was pre-empted when Bourdain presented his documentary ''[[Jeremiah Tower]], The Last Magnificent'', exploring America's first celebrity chef.

