 |OriginalAirDate={{Start date|2007|7|30}}
 |ShortSummary=Bourdain heads back to China and visits Shanghai, a budding economic superpower, where he discovers that Shanghai is considered the dumpling capital of the world made famous by its [[Xiaolongbao|soup dumpling]]. Bourdain then heads to Yunnan province. In Dali, he learns from the Bai ethnic minority people a unique way of catching fish. From there, he works his way north to Lijiang, then to Zhongdian, an ethnically Tibetan area, in search of the valley of [[Shangri-La]] as described in British author [[James Hilton (novelist)|James Hilton]]'s novel ''[[Lost Horizon]]''. The Lijiang/Zhongdian area is believed by many to have been the inspiration for the mythical Shangri-la.
